WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.291 --> 00:00:03.712
We're in Pauli Murray
College and it's sunny,

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:05.255
it's a perfect night.

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:09.092
[choir warming up and
singing chord]

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:15.598
[choir sings "Glimpse Elation"
by Derrick Skye]

00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:20.812 align:start position:0% line:48%
(Epongue)
Project 14 is a
collaboration of the Glee Club,

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:23.898 align:start position:0% line:53%
the Yale Symphony Orchestra
and the Yale Bands,

00:00:23.898 --> 00:00:26.651 align:start position:0% line:53%
which is multiple
groups in itself.

00:00:26.651 --> 00:00:30.697
[singing]

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:36.995
Collaborating together
across ensembles to perform

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:40.498
14 works within the 14
residential colleges, at Yale.

00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:45.003
[snapping fingers and singing]

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.843
Being back on campus
and performing with

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:56.055
my friends and peers
was incredibly cathartic.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:59.476
A huge part of playing in
the ensemble is being physically

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:02.812
close and feeling
the energy from the people

00:01:02.812 --> 00:01:04.522
who are nearest to you.

00:01:04.522 --> 00:01:06.524
[snapping fingers and singing]

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:08.985
[clapping and singing]

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:12.280
To have these performances
in the residential colleges

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.823
rather than Woolsey Hall,

00:01:13.823 --> 00:01:17.076
I think makes classical music
and new music

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:21.664
much more accessible,
brings exposure to people

00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:23.249
who aren't musicians.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.835
[flute plays]

00:01:25.835 --> 00:01:27.504
All the composers are of color.

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:30.924
There is a lack of composers
of color, of works of color

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.092
in the classical repertoire, or

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:36.596
at least they're not highlighted
as much as they should be.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:40.058
I am so excited for this project

00:01:40.058 --> 00:01:44.521
just to be the beginning of
repertoire by people of color,

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:45.688
by people who are alive.

00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:50.026
[instruments being played]

00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:54.489
I would hope that someone would
come up to me and say like,

00:01:55.073 --> 00:01:56.115
"that was so cool,

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:57.826 size:88% position:44%
I've never heard
anything like that."

00:01:57.826 --> 00:01:59.536
That's the kind of music
that I personally

00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:03.289
like to perform, things
that push the boundaries

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:07.544
of music and what
is culturally acceptable.

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:10.171
[choir ends song]

